.ts:286:// (its outcome reverts to `unknown`). Same-turn counterparts are skipped: they\npackages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/materialize.ts:28:// byte-identical repeats are the test for any sneaky Date.now()).\npackages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/sweep.ts:8:// drainSettled/polling in this module is a contract violation (anti-shim;\npackages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/sweep.ts:37:// the first \":\"), never the prose after it (anti-shim: no string-matching on\npackages/lhc/src/shared/derivation.ts:82:  // from model output. The deterministic provider never sets it.\npackages/lhc/src/shared/derivation.ts:176:// unchanged — the deterministic test default) or `inference` (host\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:30:// mocked transaction object.\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:38:// recordedAt is sourced deterministically for the public SDK contract proof —\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:63:// The skip set is read at transaction start and reads only the key column:\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:70:    const placeholders = chunk.map(() => \"?\").join(\", \");\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:72:      .prepare(`SELECT idempotency_key FROM event WHERE idempotency_key IN (${placeholders})`)\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:101:  // not a skip (validation-before-idempotency precedence).\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:144:    // second, the pinned order. It runs in both host modes (deterministic and\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:155:    // sets when it records a turn_end (skipped duplicates never set it, so a\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:190:    const skipSet = recordedKeys(\npackages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:195:    // so skips consume no order numbers and the se