read shows the record changed (next-compact visibility).\\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/02-smart-compact.md:55:The view comes into existence here. Compact is the only writer of the snapshot (`thread_view` + `thread_view_band`, singleton, delete-then-insert in one transaction) and one of exactly two writers of the boundary (reset; the other writer is Story 4's advance). Pull — Story 1's code, unmodified in shape — starts serving snapshot + tail the moment a view row exists. The sweep step is **absent** this story: the receipt's `sweep` field reports a literal `absent` placeholder, and Story 3 replaces it with `SweepReceipt | { skipped: true }`.\\npackages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts:47:  visibility?: Partial<VisibilityBudgets>; // defaults: 32000 / 24000 / 8000\\npackages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts:55:  visibility: VisibilityBudgets;\\npackages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts:75://   | tool_result (at-or-behind boundary)| user      | `[tool result · <name> · abridged]\\\\n<summary or deterministic truncation>` (short-form ladder) |\\npackages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts:104:  visibility: { zoneTokens: number; maxTokens: number };\\npackages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts:89:        (db.prepare(`SELECT position FROM view_boundary`).get() as { position: number | bigint })\\npackages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts:247:  it(\\\"tool_result at-or-behind the boundary: abridged marker plus short form (boundary seeded below-SDK)\\\", async () => {\\npackages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts:262:    // passes through whole), with the abridged marker and the record pointer.\\npackages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts:265:      content: `[tool result · read_file · abridged]\\\\nmapping output [full content in record §${result.messageId}]`,\\npackages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts:306:      (form) => form.form === \\\"tool_result_summary\\\" && form.state === \\\"ready\\\",\\npackages/lhc/test/view-pull.test.ts:321:    // Behind: short form — the ready summary verbatim, abridged marke