{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CYLfoVTSszf7ZT2wns21PP","type":"tool_result","content":"8:import { afterEach, describe, expect, it } from \"vitest\";\n22:// G2 leg runs the 64k/32k defaults instead.\n117:describe(\"TC-5.1 (AC-5.1, AC-5.2): the advance runs only at turn close; eviction is whole-turn, oldest-first\", () => {\n118:  it(\"holds position and bytes through mid-turn batches past max, advances exactly once at close, flips whole oldest turns\", async () => {\n179:  it(\"evicts a turnless tool result as a singleton group\", async () => {\n209:describe(\"TC-5.2 (AC-5.3, AC-5.4): peek-ahead landing, newest-turn protection, two-field config\", () => {\n210:  it(\"golden G2: 30k/25k/20k/15k turns under the 64k/32k defaults advance past the 25k group and land the zone at 35k\", async () => {\n220:      { results: [30000] },\n241:  it(\"advances through a turn when the remaining sum is exactly target (≥, not >)\", async () => {\n257:  it(\"never evicts the newest closed turn, even when it alone exceeds target and max\", async () => {\n276:  it(\"never evicts the newest closed turn when a legal trailing turnless singleton sits after it\", async () => {\n317:  it(\"holds the boundary when the only closed turn is oversized: no candidate exists\", async () => {\n325:  it(\"rejects maxTokens ≤ targetTokens at construction with a TypeError naming the constraint\", () => {\n337:  it(\"resolves the two-field defaults to 64k/32k\", () => {\n343:describe(\"TC-5.3 (AC-5.5): remaining Epic 03 contracts under the new trigger\", () => {\n344:  it(\"keeps flipped results flipped across later turn closes and replays the same trajectory from the same record\", async () => {\n===construction===\n43:describe(\"TC-1.1: provider XOR inference (AC-1.1)\", () => {\n44:  it(\"both provider and inference is a TypeError naming the XOR rule\", () => {\n56:  it(\"neither provider nor inference is a TypeError naming the XOR rule\", () => {\n63:describ