{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01BBAmZw9LdcGbrsaN9y9gbG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All review legs are complete: epic artifacts read, all six stories' implementation audited, cross-story drift checked, production path swept, both gates run green, and the keyed-run receipt verified in the impl log. Final verdict follows.\n\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n  \"crossStoryFindings\": [\n    \"Stories 2–4 compose into one coherent inference layer that matches the tech-design interface definitions verbatim: inference/types.ts carries the ModelCall contract exactly as specified, classify.ts is the AC-3.1 table plus safeCall containment, adapter.ts is the five-step pipeline (bound → render → safeCall → empty-output reject → provenance-stamped result), and sdk.ts validates XOR-then-assignments by iterating the exported FORM_KINDS set rather than a second literal list.\",\n    \"The provenance chain is consistent across story boundaries: the adapter stamps the three config-known assignment strings (src/inference/adapter.ts:91-99), messages handlers copy via the shared landForm helper (src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts:68-70), and turns handlers copy on all four turn/chunk forms (src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:103, 122-124, 201-203). The deterministic provider never sets it. No site authors provenance from model output.\",\n    \"The Story 3 reason-format deviation (retryable failures formatted 'provider_failure: <kind>: <message>' to satisfy both the TC-2.3 exhaustion shape and Epic 02's immutable verbatim-copy contract; terminal kinds kind-led) was ruled, recorded in team-impl-log.md, and is consumed consistently by Story 4's classification tests — no drift between the stories that share the format.\",\n    \"The cross-epic diff (e3be580..HEAD) is confined to the tech design's module list: scheduler.ts, tech-utils/work-queue, drain, and states appear nowhere in the diff, structurally proving DD-3's 'queue machinery unchanged' claim rather than asserting it.\",\n    \"Story 6's turn-end gate composes cleanly with the Epic 03 registration site: same onCommit slot, advance-before-poke order, and throw isolation preserved; the gate flag is set only when a turn_end is actually recorded, so skipped duplicate turn_ends never trigger an advance (src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:152-168, 219).\",\n    \"verify and verify-all now resolve to identical compositions (red-verify + full vitest) since the process-suite gate left and the inference suite is env-gated inside the default runner — consistent with the tech design's Flow 6 script rewrite; both ran green for this review.\"\n  ],\n  \"architectureFindings\": [\n    \"The inference/ ↛ domains/ boundary rule from the tech design is enforced mechanically in scripts/check-boundaries.mjs (inference grouped with tech-utils/shared as may-not-import-domains), and the boundaries gate passes.\",\n    \"shared/derivation.ts carries a type-only import of InferenceConfig from inference/types.ts (which itself imports FormKind from shared) — a type-level cycle, erased at build, documented in-code as intentionally one-directional at runtime. Acceptable as built; worth knowing if module boundaries tighten later.\",\n    \"DD-10/DD-11 land as designed: the zone read adds turn_id on the identical WHERE clause visibilityZoneTokens uses (the status/advance shared-query invariant stays structural), NULL turn_ids degrade to singleton groups, the peek-ahead decision is a pure function driven by goldens, and floorTokens is deleted from the type, defaults, and validation with a loud rejection naming the retirement (src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts:118-146).\",\n    \"Ruling-020's conditional landing window (protections take precedence over [target, target + one turn) when the newest closed turn or trailing turnless singletons force the zone above the window) is fully documented in tech-design.md Flow 5 and enforced by implementation and tests; epic.md AC-5.3 still states the unconditional window sentence — a wording gap, not a behavior gap (see F-EPIC-001).\",\n    \"Construction-error contract holds epic-wide: every config mistake is a TypeError naming the violated rule (XOR, missing kind, unknown kind key, unknown prompt, empty routing strings, max ≤ target), with no partial construction.\"\n  ],\n  \"epicCoverageAssessment\": [\n    \"All 22 ACs / 15 TCs are mapped and implemented: the eight test files match the test plan's suite layout exactly (inference-construction, inference-routing, inference-adapter, inference-prompts, inference-classification, inference-real, view-boundary-turn-end + amended view-boundary, retirement), and all seven prompt-rendering goldens exist in test/goldens/prompts/.\",\n    \"Story gate (pnpm run verify) and epic gate (pnpm run verify-all) both pass: 40 files, 377 passed, 9 env-gated keyed legs reported as skipped — never as passes — with exactly one visible 'NOT-RAN: real-inference (LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY unset)' accounting line, satisfying AC-4.1's no-silent-skip posture in the unkeyed CI default.\",\n    \"The integration-readiness gate has actually been exercised: team-impl-log.md records the DoD keyed-run receipt (2026-06-12, openai/gpt-4o-mini, 13/13 keyed tests passing, one 'RAN' accounting line, run twice), and the capstone asserts the full structural ladder — every kind ready with non-marker content, real-model provenance, cleared-then-ready mutation regeneration with changed content, second compact reflecting post-edit content, coherent health at each checkpoint.\",\n    \"The Epic 03 amendment ledger was applied per the spec-sanctioned path (floor legs superseded, per-intake legs inverted to mid-turn-never-moves, G1 re-cut for turn grouping, floorTokens-rejection test added) and the red-manifest regenerated (Story 6 commit 3c1b0c7).\",\n    \"Flow 6 deletion is proven three-legged as designed: the export-name snapshot in retirement.test.ts matches the SDK-only list, the manifest has no bin and no LHC_PROCESS_SUITE references, and the source scan finds zero LHC_PROVIDER/--provider references under src/ — confirmed independently by this review's own grep.\"\n  ],\n  \"productionPathFindings\": [\n    \"The production path is real end-to-end: createSdk's inference path builds createInferenceProvider over the host's ModelCall with no fake adapters, shims, or placeholder returns anywhere in src/ — the only 'placeholder' grep hits are SQL parameter placeholders. No skeleton stubs or NotImplementedError paths survive into the accepted code.\",\n    \"The deterministic provider remains in src/providers/deterministic.ts and is exported — this is spec-sanctioned (DD-12: CI-default test provider and byte-stable fixture substrate), arrives only by explicit injection, and has no default or fallback route to production: the env/flag resolution path is deleted and its absence is test-enforced.\",\n    \"All non-real ModelCall hosts (recordingCall, scriptedCall, throwingCall, hangingCall) and the OpenRouter-backed real test host live exclusively in test/fixtures/; src/ imports nothing from test/ (verified by grep), and the OpenRouter fixture uses plain fetch with no new dependencies per the NFR.\",\n    \"Six of the seven prompts are explicitly marked PRE-DIAL-IN — untuned but real, exactly the posture AC-2.3 sanctions; smoothing-v1 is the POC's settled prompt ported verbatim with its provenance documented in the module header. These are real production prompts pending dial-in, not placeholders.\",\n    \"The empty-output rule prevents the one disguised-non-real-output path: whitespace-only model text classifies as retryable empty_output and can never land a ready form (src/inference/adapter.ts:85-88).\"\n  ],\n  \"blockingFindings\": [],\n  \"nonBlockingFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F-EPIC-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"title\": \"epic.md AC-5.3 wording not yet amended for ruling-020's conditional landing window\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Ruling-020 (Story 6, flagged in team-impl-log.md for epic-review ratification) sanctioned the landing-window exception: when the newest-closed-turn protection or trailing turnless singletons after it force the zone above [target, target + one turn), the protections win and the zone lawfully stays above the window. tech-design.md Flow 5 carries the full amendment paragraph and the implementation and tests (view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts oversized-newest and trailing-turnless legs) enforce it, but epic.md AC-5.3 still reads 'The advance lands in [target, target + one turn).' unconditionally. This review ratifies ruling-020 on the merits — TC-5.2's oversized-newest leg already sanctioned over-target landing, and trailing turnless groups are structurally protected by the positional oldest-first boundary — leaving only the epic.md wording update outstanding.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/epic.md\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-5.3\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"quick-fix\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F-EPIC-002\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Type-only import cycle between shared/derivation.ts and inference/types.ts\",\n      \"evidence\": \"shared/derivation.ts imports InferenceConfig (type-only) from inference/types.ts to put it on SdkConfig, while inference/types.ts imports FormKind from shared/derivation.ts. The cycle is erased at build, documented in-code, and consistent with the tech design placing SdkConfig.inference in shared; no action required, recorded for future boundary-tightening awareness.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"packages/lhc/src/shared/derivation.ts\",\n        \"packages/lhc/src/inference/types.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unresolvedItems\": [\n    \"Ruling-020 is ratified by this review; the epic.md AC-5.3 wording update it called for remains outstanding (tracked as F-EPIC-001).\",\n    \"Dial-in backfill: tuned prompts and model choices must backfill this pack before final acceptance per the epic's own deferred-items contract — a declared deferral, not a defect; the provenance stamps and config-only prompt selection the dial-in period needs are in place.\"\n  ],\n  \"gateResult\": \"pass\"\n}"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3622,"cache_read_input_tokens":129077,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3622},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"40f6c7de-865c-49b2-84c6-8862983c5a5a","uuid":"e1c1d06c-8865-4e01-8a8f-5e4c5cf5a146","request_id":"req_011CbzK9fW3FfcZXvZ4bcoY5"}
