\"epic.md AC-5.3 wording not yet amended for ruling-020's conditional landing window\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Ruling-020 (Story 6, flagged in team-impl-log.md for epic-review ratification) sanctioned the landing-window exception: when the newest-closed-turn protection or trailing turnless singletons after it force the zone above [target, target + one turn), the protections win and the zone lawfully stays above the window. tech-design.md Flow 5 carries the full amendment paragraph and the implementation and tests (view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts oversized-newest and trailing-turnless legs) enforce it, but epic.md AC-5.3 still reads 'The advance lands in [target, target + one turn).' unconditionally. This review ratifies ruling-020 on the merits — TC-5.2's oversized-newest leg already sanctioned over-target landing, and trailing turnless groups are structurally protected by the positional oldest-first boundary — leaving only the epic.md wording update outstanding.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/epic.md\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-5.3\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"quick-fix\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F-EPIC-002\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Type-only import cycle between shared/derivation.ts and inference/types.ts\",\n      \"evidence\": \"shared/derivation.ts imports InferenceConfig (type-only) from inference/types.ts to put it on SdkConfig, while inference/types.ts imports FormKind from shared/derivation.ts. The cycle is erased at build, documented in-code, and consistent with the tech design placing SdkConfig.inference in shared; no action required, recorded for future boundary-tightening awareness.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"packages/lhc/src/shared/derivation.ts\",\n        \"packages/lhc/src/inference/types.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\